
# Business Requirements Document (BRD)

## 1. Document Information

- **Project Name:** AI-Assisted Clinical Documentation Workflow Improvement
- **Document Type:** Business Requirements Document
- **Version:** 1.0
- **Status:** Draft — Portfolio Project
- **Domain:** Healthcare IT

## 2. Business Background

Clinical documentation involves converting consultation information into structured clinical notes. Manual preparation may require repetitive typing, corrections, and additional time to complete documentation.

This project proposes an AI-assisted workflow that generates a draft clinical note for clinician review and approval.

## 3. Problem Statement

The existing manual documentation process may create documentation delays, repetitive work, and opportunities for incomplete or inconsistent information. The project aims to analyze these challenges and define a proposed workflow that supports documentation efficiency while retaining clinician oversight.

The current-state assumptions must be validated with relevant stakeholders before real-world implementation.

## 4. Business Objectives

1. Reduce manual effort involved in preparing clinical notes.
2. Improve the completeness and consistency of documentation.
3. Reduce avoidable corrections and repeated work.
4. Ensure clinicians review and approve notes before finalization.
5. Protect patient information through appropriate security and access controls.

## 5. Project Scope

### In Scope

- Analyze the current documentation workflow.
- Gather and document business requirements.
- Identify gaps in the existing process.
- Propose an AI-assisted documentation workflow.
- Define functional requirements and business rules.
- Create user stories and acceptance criteria.
- Define UAT scenarios and performance indicators.

### Out of Scope

- Developing a production AI application.
- Connecting to a live EHR system.
- Using real patient data.
- Claiming actual efficiency improvements without testing.
- Replacing clinician review or approval.

## 6. Stakeholders

| Stakeholder               | Responsibility                                           |
| ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| Doctor / Clinician        | Reviews, edits, and approves clinical notes              |
| Medical Scribe            | Supports documentation and identifies workflow issues    |
| Practice Manager          | Reviews operational efficiency                           |
| IT / EHR Team             | Assesses technical feasibility and integration           |
| Compliance / Privacy Team | Reviews privacy and security requirements                |
| Business Analyst          | Gathers requirements and documents the proposed solution |
| AI Development Team       | Evaluates and develops the proposed functionality        |

## 7. Business Requirements

| ID    | Requirement                                                                                   | Priority |
| ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |
| BR-01 | The solution should support faster clinical note preparation.                                 | High     |
| BR-02 | The solution should generate structured draft notes from authorized consultation information. | High     |
| BR-03 | A clinician must review and approve the note before finalization.                             | Critical |
| BR-04 | The clinician must be able to edit and correct generated content.                             | High     |
| BR-05 | Patient information must be protected through appropriate security controls.                  | Critical |
| BR-06 | Approved notes should be saved to the correct EHR record through an authorized workflow.      | High     |
| BR-07 | The solution should support measurement of documentation quality and efficiency.              | Medium   |

## 8. Business Success Metrics

The following indicators can be used to evaluate the solution after implementation and testing:

- Average clinical note completion time.
- Percentage of notes requiring significant corrections.
- Percentage of required note sections completed.
- Time between draft generation and clinician approval.
- Number of incomplete or pending notes.

Baseline measurements and improvement targets must be established with stakeholders. No performance results are claimed in this conceptual project.

## 9. Assumptions and Dependencies

- The organization authorizes the proposed AI documentation workflow.
- Consultation information can be provided through an approved method.
- Clinicians can review, edit, and approve generated notes.
- EHR integration or an authorized transfer method is technically feasible.
- Applicable privacy, security, consent, and record-retention requirements are addressed.

## 10. Risks and Constraints

- AI-generated content may be inaccurate or incomplete.
- Incorrect patient or encounter selection could create documentation risks.
- EHR integration may require additional technical work.
- Privacy and security requirements may restrict available input methods.
- Users may require training before adopting the proposed workflow.

## 11. Business Acceptance Criteria

The proposed solution will be considered ready for business acceptance when:

1. Agreed business requirements have been reviewed by stakeholders.
2. The draft can be reviewed and corrected by an authorized clinician.
3. Required clinician approval is enforced before finalization.
4. The workflow handles saving failures without falsely reporting success.
5. Security, privacy, and access-control requirements have been reviewed.
6. Agreed UAT scenarios have been executed and their results documented.

## 12. Approval

This document is a draft created for an educational Business Analyst portfolio project. Stakeholder review and formal approval would be required before implementation in a real healthcare environment.
